@page "/tables/advanced-table/loading-mode"

@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Switch
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.AdvancedTable.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.AdvancedTable.Components.Columns

<DescriptionBanner>
    The table supports two loading modes:
    <strong>Virtualize</strong> renders only visible rows (efficient for large datasets),
    while <strong>Load All</strong> renders every row at once.

    Virtualization only has an effect when the table's height is limited — by <code>MaximumHeight</code>, by a rule
    for <code>CssClass</code>, or by the parent layout. Otherwise every row is laid out and there is nothing to
    virtualize. Toggle below to switch.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="options">
    <div class="option">
        <label>Virtualize table</label>
        <Switch @bind-Value="_virtualize" />
    </div>
</div>

<h3>Limited by <code>MaximumHeight</code></h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    The table grows with its rows up to <code>300px</code>, then scrolls internally. A percentage only takes effect
    when the table's parent has a definite height.
</DescriptionBanner>

<AdvancedTable ItemsProvider="_itemsProvider" RowClickSelectionEnabled="false" Mode="@LoadingMode" MaximumHeight="300px">
    <Columns>
        <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Id" Title="Id">
            <CellContent>@context.Id</CellContent>
        </AdvancedTableColumn>
        <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Key" Title="Key">
            <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
        </AdvancedTableColumn>
        <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Value" Title="Value">
            <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
        </AdvancedTableColumn>
        <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp">
            <CellContent>@context.Timestamp</CellContent>
        </AdvancedTableColumn>
    </Columns>
</AdvancedTable>

<h3>Sized by the parent layout through <code>CssClass</code></h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    The table fills the space a flex column leaves below a fixed-height block. <code>flex: 1</code> makes it take that
    space, and <code>min-height: 0</code> lets it shrink below the height of its rows — without it, a flex item never
    becomes smaller than its content. The rule reaches the table with <code>::deep</code> from the page's own markup.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="flex-column">
    <div class="above-table">Fixed-height content above the table</div>

    <AdvancedTable ItemsProvider="_itemsProvider" RowClickSelectionEnabled="false" Mode="@LoadingMode" CssClass="filling-table">
        <Columns>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Id" Title="Id">
                <CellContent>@context.Id</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Key" Title="Key">
                <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Value" Title="Value">
                <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp">
                <CellContent>@context.Timestamp</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
        </Columns>
    </AdvancedTable>
</div>
